ally let me do: reset_emulator, then play_input combining title navigation + right run. That ends with the game running. Then immediately call pause_emulator (next message) — but between, the game runs maybe 1-3 seconds and Mario could get hit by the Goomba. Risky but earlier the immediate screenshot after the run showed him alive; the death took longer.\n\nBetter: end the play_input script with the game in a state where Mario is safe: not needed; just pause quickly.\n\nActually, there's a neat trick: after the right run, the game continues, but if I include [buttons:[], frames:1] it doesn't help.\n\nLet me just do reset, then play_input with title nav + right 150, then pause immediately.\n\nActually — even better: I can include the pause by making the emulator paused BEFORE the play_input. Let me do reset_emulator and pause_emulator in the SAME message (both independent-ish; if reset unpauses then pause after... order matters). Tools in one block are executed in order I believe. But to be safe, do reset, get result, then pause, then play.\n\nLet me minimize: call reset_emulator and screenshot together. Then decide."}
