e one byte at 0xC8C from 0x53 to something else and see if the ? block's top-left tile changes.\n\nBut careful: this table might be used by many blocks (the ? block and also bricks?). The two identical entries 0xC8C and 0xC90 — maybe one is for ? blocks and one for something else.\n\nWe should identify which entry the ? block uses. Approach: write 0xC8C to a different tile (e.g. 0x3C or 0x24) and reset+get to the ? block and screenshot. Actually reset + attract demo shows 1-1 but the ? block may be off screen at start. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, we can prove by editing while the ? block is on screen: write prgRom byte, then... but the nametable was already built at level load, so changing PRG won't change the current screen. We'd need to reload the level (reset and walk again) — costly.\n\nHmm, the task says: \"Prove each origin by a ledgered write_memory to prgRom of one byte there (with a reason), reset_emulator, and a screenshot showing the predicted change\".\n\nSo we need the ? block visible after reset. After reset → title/attract demo. In the attract demo, the camera starts at 0 and Mario stands. The ? block at level x 256 is off-screen. Hmm. But maybe the attract demo plays a bit? On the title screen, SMB shows the demo where Mario runs? Actually the \"attract demo\" is the title screen with Mario standing? Hmm, earlier the first screenshot showed Mario at start of 1-1 with no ? block visible; TIME 391. The attract demo in SMB1 (title screen) shows Mario standing at the start? Actually the SMB title screen shows a demo where Mario walks right and jumps? No, in the NES SMB the title screen shows just the logo and Mario standing; the demo gameplay plays after the title times out? Hmm.\n\nWait, our very first screenshot showed a HUD with WORLD 1-1 TIME 391 and Mario standing at the start, no logo. That's the \"attract demo\" (gameplay demo) that runs when the title screen is idle. In that demo, does Mario move? In SMB1 the attract demo (after title) shows Mario run